<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-MAY					     .</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-MAY					     .</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Marie, with 75 mph winds, is in the open waters of the western Pacific near 18.1n/159.8e, moving north at 10 mph. This track will continue while Marie strengthens during the next 36 hours. This system is a significant threat to shipping.  </p>
<p>There are no other statements at this time.</p>
</text>
